{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded","id":1257400,"title":"How could a solar queen use and treat Dragonblooded?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-26T10:51:23-07:00","id":1257400,"title":"How could a solar queen use and treat Dragonblooded?","content":"Um, yeah, title pretty much describes my question.<br /> <br /> The players are Dragonblooded and to my surprise have decided to join a solar queen. I'm unsure how to proceed now. Especially the position of the Dragonblooded in the kingdom and how a solar would use and treat them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5592-alonne","name":"Alonne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5592_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T11:05:51-07:00","id":1257402,"title":"","content":"I think it really depends on her. Solars are individuals, it probably depends on her background, socio-cultural upbringing, the geopolitics of the region, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> There's no Solar school where they learn to treat Dragonblood a particular way.<br /> <br /> Does this Solar have any other allies? If she's not part of a circle, the PCs may well be her most powerful allies, so she's probably going to want to treat them well.<br /> <br /> Are these Dragonblood dynasts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T11:35:04-07:00","id":1257408,"title":"","content":"She's not part of a circle and has sorcerer and two other mortal kings as allies <br /> <br /> It is a mixed group of dynasts and outcastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5592-alonne","name":"Alonne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5592_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T13:06:37-07:00","id":1257424,"title":"","content":"What is the Solar Queen\u2019s background? What Caste is she?<br /> <br /> Is she the ruler of a Satrapy, subordinate to the Realm? Is she a figurehead with a council that runs things? Or is she a true absolute monarch?<br /> <br /> Was she born among the noble class or was she a peasant? Did she plot and scheme to gain the throne, did she take it by force of arms, or was she just born into the position?<br /> <br /> Where do her skills lie? Administration? Socialization? The Military? Trade? Being so pretty that everyone just does whatever she wants? Is she secretly a ninja?<br /> <br /> Why did the PCs sign on with her? Do they want to support her ambitions in taking over the world? They just really like this nation of hers? They failed to defend against her solar magic and now they have defining intimacies of love towards her? <br /> <br /> If you\u2019re not sure what the players want from this game, it\u2019s ok to ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T16:17:10-07:00","id":1257459,"title":"","content":"It is an absolute monarchy. She was born as a daughter of the previous queen and got the throne through a civil war where her other siblings were either killed or exiled. The queen is a Zenith. Especially skilled in socialization and intrigue, but also quite good at fighting and leading people.<br /> <br /> As far as I understand, they want to be part of an ascending (solar) empire. And for a change they want to fight with and not against a solar. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5592-alonne","name":"Alonne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5592_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T16:33:38-07:00","id":1257463,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t forget the most important factor here: How much possibility for friction do you want between them and her? *evil grin*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T17:03:33-07:00","id":1257468,"title":"","content":"Also an important point would be what are the backgrounds of the DBs? A bunch of outcastes or lost eggs a solar might be willing to trust when they sign on, but you get a few scions from a Great House and well frack ever trusting that without a method to kill them at a moment's notice in case of sudden betrayal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T17:46:47-07:00","id":1257473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded?p=1257468#post1257468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but you get a few scions from a Great House and well frack ever trusting that without a method to kill them at a moment's notice in case of sudden betrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t really see the difference, outcastes can still be a Wyld Hunt in disguise. Heck, the dynasts are the ones who could say \u201cYou can trust me because the second my family finds out I\u2019m associating with you I\u2019m dead or worse to them and have nowhere else to go.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T18:10:41-07:00","id":1257478,"title":"","content":"The smart ruler never entirely trusts their subordinates, but a group of DBs is too useful to pass up. I would have the queen send them on a mission that seems important and gives them a great opportunity to betray her and see what happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T20:29:15-07:00","id":1257491,"title":"","content":"Two words: Giant. Mirrors.<br /> <br /> No, but seriously it would depend heavily on a lot of factors. Some things to consider.<br /> <br /> 1. How close is she to the Realm? How strong is the Immaculate Faith (and, in particular, the prohibition on Anathema) in the surrounding area? The more unstable she considers herself and the more of a regional threat Dragon-Blooded are, the more suspicious she's going to be of a group that offers to join her. Of course, at the same time, this might mean she <i>needs</i> them more.<br /> <br /> 2. What is her own history? Her own experiences? Does she believe in elements of the Immaculate Faith herself (she just doesn't think that she, personally, is Anathema, whatever it says?) Does she care a lot about the First Age and want to return to it? Does she have some sort of existing policy or position towards Dragon-Blooded, and if so, what? What's she planning to do when the Realm starts trying to eradicate her - fight them first? Reason with them? Something else?<br /> <br /> 3. Who are these Dragon-Blooded? Would she have heard of them before? Is there anyone else in her kingdom who can vouch for them, their abilities, their willingness to work honestly with her, etc? What's their background? She's naturally going to be more suspicious of Dynasts (why would they want to work under her, who they officially consider Anathema?) than Outcastes, who may not be Immaculates and are more likely to be in a situation where working for her is a step up.<br /> <br /> 4. She's going to want to interview them about a lot of these questions. Why do they want to work with her. What do they expect out of it. What their beliefs on the Immaculate Faith and Anathema are. Are they willing to fight other Dragon-Blooded (including, in the case of Dynasts, potentially their own kin) if she's attacked. Things like that.<br /> <br /> 5. In terms of their larger position in the kingdom, a lot of it extends from this. Dragon-Blooded will be recognized as Exalted princes of the earth almost everywhere (unless this Solar Queen has done a <i>lot</i> of work to stamp that out in her region, or it's someplace totally disconnected from broader regional cultures.) That said, the further you get from the Realm and the main centers of the Immaculate Faith, the less effusive this respect becomes and the more it shifts towards just viewing them as magic-users with special powers. You also have to ask the related question of how the region views its Solar Queen - is she liked? Respected? Feared? Hated? The locals will judge the players based on their association with her (and possibly re-evaluate their opinion of her based on her association with them, if they see the cooperation of Dragon-Blooded as a sign that she's a &quot;genuine&quot; Exalt and not Anathema.) Conversely, people who hate, fear, or distrust her may expect the Dragon-Blooded to &quot;save&quot; them from her, and feel betrayed when it becomes clear the DB are genuinely working with her.<br /> <br /> Of course, all of this depends on her own personality and beliefs. Depending on who she is, her response could be anything from &quot;yay, new friends! Here's some stuff I'd totally love if you could help me with!&quot; to &quot;nice try, Realm spies! GANK.&quot; (If you haven't established her character yet, I would obviously lean more towards the former in the interests of giving your players the sort of game they seem to want.)<br /> <br /> But you might talk to them a bit about their expectations, too. You don't have to sit there wondering &quot;why are my players doing this?&quot;, you can just ask them, since it will help you plan ahead a bit better.<br /> <br /> If you're asking what sorts of quests and adventures she might have for them... again, some of it depends on this, but unless she's really far into the hinterlands, having DB supporters would be helpful to her in terms of shoring up her own rule (since mortals who might have accused her of being Anathema are less likely to do so when she has obvious Dragon-Blooded working with her.) So she would want to have them do big ostentatious deeds in her name. If your players want a more adventure / combat-oriented campaign, this could be fighting rogue gods and other threats, putting down rebellions (or trying to defuse them non-violently), hunting bandits, going around passing judgment in her name, etc; if they want a more social one, it could be acting as members of her court, attending balls, negotiating treaties, etc. Using them as diplomats would be inherently very appealing to her because people who might otherwise refuse to treat with Anathema will have more trouble ignoring or insulting Princes of the Earth acting in her name.<br /> <br /> Of course, this also depends on the skills of the DBs in question - if they're good crafters, she'd set them crafting, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 09-27-2018, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T21:33:04-07:00","id":1257497,"title":"","content":"Assuming the Hearth can convince her their intentions are true, that's the kind of elite guardians a monarch would be crazy to pass up. The hearth becoming her preferred enforcers is ripe with story seeds. You can easily add intrigue by her original right hand becoming jealous/suspicious of the PCs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T00:41:30-07:00","id":1257514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alonne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded?p=1257459#post1257459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understand, they want to be part of an ascending (solar) empire. And for a change they want to fight with and not against a solar. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like she would make great a Boss NPC. (Not as in a video game boss, but as in the person who's in charge and sends the PCs on missions and gives them responsibilities).<br /> Ruling/expanding an empire is hard, and having Exalts that can use their expertise in dealing with the many different problems that can arise from it, sounds like a great set up for a story.<br /> <br /> Wether it's dealing with uprisings from within the empire, diplomatic missions, or classic quest-style adventures to clear surrounding lands from natural or supernatural problems, solo missions or missions as a group, I think you'll be able to find ways to play up, and cater to, the PCs both as individuals and as a group.<br /> <br /> Exalted lends itself well to shifting scope from the small (a fight to root out an enemy hiding in the basement of a tavern in the shady parts of town) to the larger (directing a citywide investigation or leading a spy network). Going from one to the other, and using small downtime segments could probably really help establish the players as powerplayers in the empire, and give them reasons to care about it, as well as the queen.<br /> Then you could bring out the really big threats: A dark cult, with ties to a local shadowland, is discovered to have spread inside the empire. How high up does it go? / An outside force is gathering and war is on the horizon. Maybe an old Lunar with an ancient grudge has gathered their circle to crush the ascending empire before it grows out of control. Or The Realm has decided it poses too much of a threat (maybe pushed by the houses that the the dynasts among the PCs abandoned) / It is discovered that the empire has reflection somewhere in the wyld, an empire of horrors and nightmare soldiers that grows and shrinks in accordance to the empire of the Solar Queen. Led by a being of terrifying magnificence and power, with a number of dreaded lieutenants (corresponding with the number of PCs), and as it grows in power the threat of it breaking through to Creation, also grows. How do the PCs respond to finding this out?<br /> <br /> Aaaaanyway, that's just some thoughts and ideas from me, on the situation. Not sure if that's helpful or not :/<br /> But hopefully!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T01:23:28-07:00","id":1257523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alonne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded?p=1257459#post1257459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an absolute monarchy. She was born as a daughter of the previous queen and got the throne through a civil war where her other siblings were either killed or exiled. The queen is a Zenith. Especially skilled in socialization and intrigue, but also quite good at fighting and leading people.<br /> <br /> As far as I understand, they want to be part of an ascending (solar) empire. And for a change they want to fight with and not against a solar. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>With her, but against <i>whom</i>? Consider what common enemies might help them forge an uneasy alliance and hold it together long enough for trust to be built.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 09-27-2018, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T01:40:33-07:00","id":1257525,"title":"","content":"Make the players her crack team of &quot;trouble-shooters&quot; - they're her top agents who go out and deal with unruly spirits, raiding warlords and other &quot;small scale&quot; issues that isn't big enough for her to pay attention to.<br /> <br /> ...and then maybe set up a system to allow the players to call in the queen in case they get into trouble, to make the players appreciate that they have a heavy-hitter to call on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T05:27:02-07:00","id":1257551,"title":"","content":"If there ever was one, this is the game to explore Solar Limit Break and the Great Curse.<br /> <br /> Have Queenie be genuinely grateful for their loyalty and vision in signing on to her cause. Have her rely on them, while she handles affairs of state and faith, and have her join them for the toughest of battles.<br /> <br /> But along the way, her frustrations build and manifest. She has her first Break in their presence, and because of them being there, she exerts her will to bottle it up. <br /> <br /> But subsequent breaks aren't always with the Circle around. Sometimes they come back from a mission to find that she's done something awful, or broken down into a blubbering heap. Or both. The Circle has to deal with the fallout and hold the kingdom together.<br /> <br /> At the turning point of the overall story, the Circle finds out that not only is Queenie subject to a terrifying Limit condition, but that a dreadful and subtle enemy has been manipulating conditions around her to prod her weakness. This means that they not only have to deal with that enemy, but with the knowledge that other, experienced and dangerous Celestials, have greater lore about the Curse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T08:18:50-07:00","id":1257576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alonne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded#post1257400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The players are Dragonblooded <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Then it would seem to me that they're the far more important part of the equation. Tell me about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T09:48:21-07:00","id":1257586,"title":"","content":"Questions about the Queen:<br /> <br /> 1) How does she feel about the Immaculate Faith?<br /> 2) How does she feel about hereditary aristocracies?<br /> 3) How does she feel about powerful potential rivals?<br /> 4) What can't she get done with her existing resources?<br /> <br /> Questions about your players (which as Isator mentioned is the more important thing):<br /> <br /> 1) How much do they like intrigue?<br /> 2) How much do they like taking the initiative vs. being given &quot;missions&quot; by some kind of boss figure?<br /> 3) How much would they enjoy playing a role in the development/management of the kingdom as a whole?<br /> 4) What was their reason for joining this queen in general? In particular, what seemed to be the appeal to them out of character, if any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3457-matthias","name":"Matthias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T18:04:19-07:00","id":1257696,"title":"","content":"How does she use them? As befits their skillsets. The fighty ones are leading armies, turning battles and smiting demons, the sneaky ones are spying and assassinating, the social ones are using their position as the Only Acceptable Exalted to spread her influence, or subvert local tenets of the Faith toward her ends,<br /> <br /> Remember, most DBs have more clout than even a divinely skilled orator. If she needs ships, she can likely manage to get them, but not subtly - a greatly persuasive ruler deciding to overawe the harbormaster of Greyfalls will definitely get the job done, but so will &quot;my surname is Peleps and I have jade&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also? A Solar is greatly powerful in personal combat <i>when they can take the gloves off</i>. If it's important that nobody knows she's a Solar (and it should be) then she only really has 13 motes or so on hand, because she cannot afford to start glowing. A DB that can go all-out is a much more effective champion than a Solar with one hand tied behind her back.<br /> <br /> 'Cause if it becomes known that a Solar has absolute dominion over a growing Threshold state? The Wyld Hunt will ring every single alarm bell and excrete entire ziggurats worth of bricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","user":"Amayad","date":". 09-27-2018, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24387-amayad","name":"Amayad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T14:32:56-07:00","id":1258036,"title":"","content":"Ever heard of the First Age? The Queen would make em the heads of their own clans and would breed em! She could also use Sorcery to make her own Wonderland...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T17:00:10-07:00","id":1258078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded?p=1258036#post1258036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever heard of the First Age? The Queen would make em the heads of their own clans and would breed em! She could also use Sorcery to make her own Wonderland...</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot the sarcasm indicator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThe very existence of flame-throwers proves that some time, somewhere, someone said to themselves, You know, I want to set those people over there on fire, but I'm just not close enough to get the job done.\u201d George Carlin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123-trax","name":"Trax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar123_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T17:54:18-07:00","id":1258085,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking about how well What Fire Has Wrought did, with individual and groups of Terrestrials whose aspirations and applications were very specific and personal, rather vague or generic.<br /> <br /> There are so many things that Dragon Blooded can be and do, and so many of them to cover such possibilities* that the question of &quot;what can this Solar do with a bunch of them&quot; is not providing nearly enough information to form a useful answer. My God, I don't even know their Aspects!<br /> <br /> * Some of the larger Great Houses might have more Exalted in them than all non-Terrestrials combined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T00:28:26-07:00","id":1258131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alonne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded#post1257400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, yeah, title pretty much describes my question.<br /> <br /> The players are Dragonblooded and to my surprise have decided to join a solar queen. I'm unsure how to proceed now. Especially the position of the Dragonblooded in the kingdom and how a solar would use and treat them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Judging from your surprise, it sounds like you set her up to be an antagonist? Has she done anything especially negative in the area? Do the PCs really know anything about her or it's just the players want to do something different regardless?<br /> <br /> As to the question, as noted, Exalted allies of any sort are insanely useful...but also insanely dangerous. She'd be a fool to trust them off the bat. Does she have some way of verifying loyalty, like Judge's Ear to ensure they're telling the truth? If she were Eclipse, she could oath-bind them, but that's not an option, unless it's not too late to change her caste...<br /> <br /> So, assuming they approach peacefully, and announce their intentions to join her, I'd have her accept their offer...provisionally. Which means they are under constant supervision, from guides and spies. She sends them out on a few missions, designed to test their loyalties, esp for the former Dynasts, against the Realm. Should they prove themselves worthy, she lets them into her inner council, and makes good use of their particular talents and charms (Crafting, Sorcery, Performance to spread her propaganda, Socialize for diplomacy, etc). <br /> <br /> That's just assuming everything goes smoothly, and it's your job to ensure that it doesn't. Queenie likely has other servants who fear losing their positions to the PCs, and will do ANYthing to make sure they look bad and don't stick around. They may even work with foreign spies hoping to sabotage her dominion. And even if SHE is ok with working with ex-Dynasts, many of her citizens may bear a grudge against anyone from the Realm. Another complication might be Sidereals: If she's even loosely associated with the Gold Faction, your unIlluminated PCs may be wild cards that they don't want around...<br /> <br /> HTH!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T01:20:49-07:00","id":1258141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded?p=1258036#post1258036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever heard of the First Age?</div> </div> </div> </div>She may not have. Or at least, nothing accurate.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> To some extent there are so many variables, that I think it's really up to you to decide what would make a better game.<br /> Should she betray them?<br /> Send them on missions as a quest-giver every session?<br /> Send them to deal with her most difficult foe?<br /> Make them border-nobles? (ie they're far away, but can control an area for her that's dangerous and difficult to control)<br /> Make a true partnership with them as her top lieutenants, asking for advice and so on? Maybe marry one of them? (Or more!)<br /> <br /> All of these could make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T01:54:59-07:00","id":1258152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded?p=1258141#post1258141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She may not have. Or at least, nothing accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't all Solars supposed to have FA memories and dreams, tho? And the older and more powerful they are, the more vivid the memories/dreams are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T02:07:31-07:00","id":1258155,"title":"","content":"No. I mean, a lot of them have very, very vague memories. Not all. And those memories are not necessarily useful for knowing much about the First Age.<br /> <br /> But if you have memories of being murdered by Dragonblood at a giant feast of Solars... that just tells you Solars were murdered by Dragonblood at a big feast. It doesn't give you much context. Similarly, if you remember fighting a horde of golems alongside a giant boar-man, or hanging out in a giant golden temple floating above a forest that stretches to the horizon while supping on the finest wines... that'll indicate you were very powerful in your previous life, but it doesn't tell you much about the social organisation of Dragonblood during the First Age. Or even how long ago this was. <br /> <br /> And I don't remember anything about the memories getting more vivid with age and power (though Dragonkings do!). Just that, as you live longer, you'll probably remember more.<br /> <br /> Really, it's up to the ST+players how much they want in terms of First Age memories. But they're certainly not enough to give you accurate historical knowledge of the First Age (unlike 2nd ed Infernals, whose memories were much, much clearer, and so did give them mechanical bonuses on First Age craft and history).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T06:22:27-07:00","id":1258186,"title":"","content":"Yeah 3e has made some pretty serious efforts to mitigate the role of past life memories as integral to the Solar experience.<br /> <br /> Resonance with all magic materials makes it less essential to find your FA panopoly.<br /> Lore has a context requirement and the rules don't talk about legendary successes, so there's less pulling information out of the aethyr to justify with past lives.<br /> Martial Arts exist at mortal level, you don't exalt and instinctively enter a fighting stance that died out thousands of years ago unless that's compelling for you.<br /> <br /> I'm pleased that it took to page 2 to get to breeding the Dragon-Blooded and that seems to be in jest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 09-30-2018, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T14:34:22-07:00","id":1258268,"title":"","content":"When I think about how an NPC is going to act, I consider a few things. <br /> <br /> First and foremost is what helps my players tell their stories. This includes direct assistance to player goals, and obstacles that players can overcome or define themselves against. <br /> <br /> The second thing I consider is what's already been established about a character; NPC's need to strike a balance between never changing regardless of what players do, and changing to suit the players with no resistance at all.<br /> <br /> The third thing I consider is that character's role in the setting. This affects their default assumptions, and challenges they're likely to face. In Exalted, Caste is a major part of said role.<br /> <br /> Since your players want to be part of a Solar queen's rise in prominence, to me that suggests that she should welcome their assistance, and that they should serve as enforcers, problem-solvers, diplomats, and personal confidants. A Solar can't be everywhere, and a queen should spend much of her time close to home, managing, directing, and building up her queendom. If she's forward-thinking, she'll treat them as precious not just for their skills and perspective, but also as a long-term investment in a whole <i>clan or </i><i>class</i> of powerful servants.<br /> <br /> Consider her Intimacies and other relationships. For each PC, I'd give the queen at least one Intimacy that dovetails with or clashes with one of that PC's Intimacies. She's going to be a central figure in the campaign, so she needs something to keep the PC's loyal, and something to cause some friction, so that either the PC or the queen will change their minds and grow.<br /> <br /> Since she's a Zenith, the two major elements I'd focus on are <i>faith</i> (whether in an ideal, a cause, or a god) and <i>social power</i>. People will flock to her banner, falling in line with sometimes-frightening speed. Some of those people will be <i>bad people</i>--the PC's might have to make hard decisions about whether they can support a given alliance, or work with an immoral-but-loyal servant. The queen will push her kingdom headlong into wars she deems just--and the PC's will have to decide whether the queen's justice is worth all the pain and bloodshed that the PC's will be doing much of personally. She may treasure the PC's, and take for granted that their faith is absolute, like hers is. She may assume they'll instantly agree with her, but I strongly advise <i>avoiding forceful social influence against the PC's</i> except when the queen is desperate and/or Limit Breaking. Leave most of her social interaction with the PC's unrolled, and instead simply narrate her kindness and inspiring force except when the players show interest in bringing mechanics into play. Update her Intimacies regularly, and offer players the opportunity to do so when they have dramatic interactions with her. Showcase her terrifying social power in how easily NPC's bend to her will.<br /> <br /> Finally, let the PC's enjoy the benefits. Being part of a queendom isn't just about adventure and conquest; <i>being part of something </i>is a fundamental human drive. Have PC's regularly interact with other subjects, and show the queendom they're helping to build. Show why it's worthwhile that they've done so, and let the queen heap rewards upon them for their service. Give them and their loved ones privileges that they'll fear losing. Let them have loved ones. Let the players see the queen when she's at her most glorious and imperious, and then let them see her the way mortals never get to: vulnerable, concerned, tired, maybe even petty. Let them help define the form of the idealized better world that the queen desires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T14:23:09-07:00","id":1259283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded?p=1258186#post1258186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pleased that it took to page 2 to get to breeding the Dragon-Blooded and that seems to be in jest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think that she would at least be <i>aware</i> of the hereditary nature of the DB exaltation and would keep it in mind in terms of eg. offering them titles and the like and try to encourage them to put down roots as nobility in hopes that their descendants will also be loyal to her. Depending on how her relationship with them shakes out she might suggest / offer / encourage specific strategic marriages. To the extent that she does, she would probably care more about trying to tie their bloodlines to her realm through marriage (like a real-world monarch would, really, putting aside the supernatural factor), rather than the sort of planning the Realm sometimes uses to strengthen their Exaltation. This seems appropriate to focus on if the players are interested in play a Game of Thrones sort of story where they set themselves up and found families that become major players in the region.<br /> <br /> But really that's too far in the future for her to worry too much about it. Her immediate concerns are likely to be about ensuring she lives long enough for that sort of long-term dynastic thing to matter, and if she concludes that they're only going to be with her for a while before they move on, she'll probably accept whatever help she can get from them and be grateful for it. (I mean, she'll obviously make a concerted effort to <i>convince</i> them to stay. But &quot;keep the kingdom together for the next ten years&quot; is probably a priority in the unsettled era of the Age of Sorrows.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-06-2018, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T17:25:50-07:00","id":1259488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded?p=1259283#post1259283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that she would at least be <i>aware</i> of the hereditary nature of the DB exaltation and would keep it in mind in terms of eg. offering them titles and the like and try to encourage them to put down roots as nobility in hopes that their descendants will also be loyal to her. Depending on how her relationship with them shakes out she might suggest / offer / encourage specific strategic marriages. To the extent that she does, she would probably care more about trying to tie their bloodlines to her realm through marriage (like a real-world monarch would, really, putting aside the supernatural factor), rather than the sort of planning the Realm sometimes uses to strengthen their Exaltation. This seems appropriate to focus on if the players are interested in play a Game of Thrones sort of story where they set themselves up and found families that become major players in the region.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a crucial difference in terminology here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T20:27:21-07:00","id":1259516,"title":"","content":"If you have a bunch of badass warriors who have offered to serve you but you're not sure of their loyalty... you test it by sending them after other badasses who want to kill you.<br /> <br /> Have her ask them to take out the Wyld Hunt that House Ledaal is sending after her. Include an NPC or two in the Hunt that's a friend/family member of the Dynastic PCs. If they succeed, and prove themselves more loyal to her than the Realm/their Houses, then she can start to cautiously trust them.<br /> <br /> This is a Zenith, a religious leader! Starting your own cult 101: Make them burn their bridges with friends and family so they feel they can't leave your cult to go back to their old lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T22:47:09-07:00","id":1259535,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, you don't want to push too fast. Making them fight their own relatives might erode their loyalty fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T03:26:07-07:00","id":1259561,"title":"","content":"Ecery time I see this thread bumped, I look at the title, see the words &quot;use and treat&quot;, and it always makes me think &quot;it's good to be the queen&quot; \ud83d\ude08","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T04:27:56-07:00","id":1259564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alonne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded#post1257400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, yeah, title pretty much describes my question.<br /> <br /> The players are Dragonblooded and to my surprise have decided to join a solar queen. I'm unsure how to proceed now. Especially the position of the Dragonblooded in the kingdom and how a solar would use and treat them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, how would a royal treat a guest that could be either a valuable enemy or a valuable ally, and very unlikely will be apathetic?<br /> <br /> <br /> What does she know of the dragon blooded? What can she give them? How can she entice them? How can she safeguard herself against their threat?<br /> What can they do? What is their price? How likely are they to remain loyal?<br /> What does the queen need done that would demand exalted might?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-12T09:25:52-07:00","id":1260304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded?p=1259535#post1259535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, you don't want to push too fast. Making them fight their own relatives might erode their loyalty fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably best for the Solar to send the DBs against a threat she can reasonably assume they already agree on to start with---the ravenous dead, rampaging beasts, Wyld gribblies, mortal bandits. Build up that working relationship, feel out what can be asked when and why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-12T09:30:21-07:00","id":1260305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded?p=1259564#post1259564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, how would a royal treat a guest that could be either a valuable enemy or a valuable ally, and very unlikely will be apathetic?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Just to examine that question from the other side... what if she's not entirely aware, yet, what her royal potential might be? The DB Circle might become the ones to guide her into a wise dominion, in a world full of savage and cruel influences that would otherwise guide her into tyranny. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-12T11:35:38-07:00","id":1260319,"title":"","content":"Regarding cult indoctrination: The time for &quot;pitting inductees against their loved ones&quot; is before joining, as a requirement to join in the first place (e.g. fraternities/sororities), or after a period of indoctrination through community-building. The first is only for established organizations that can plausibly say they don't need you because people are clambering to join. The latter is how you bring in valuable members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-14T04:36:28-07:00","id":1260504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1257400-how-could-a-solar-queen-use-and-treat-dragonblooded?p=1259561#post1259561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ecery time I see this thread bumped, I look at the title, see the words &quot;use and treat&quot;, and it always makes me think &quot;it's good to be the queen&quot; \ud83d\ude08</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I'm particularly pleased that it took two pages before we got some variation of &quot;make them fuck&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}